      "rev_n_1_26c3e9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_26c3e9_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_26c3e9",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a brute-force approach where we iterate over all pairs of points to determine the line passing through them and then check how many circles intersect this line. This approach is straightforward but computationally expensive.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406507.518207
      },
      "rev_n_2_ed13fa_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_ed13fa_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_ed13fa",
        "thought_text": "Utilize a geometric transformation to convert the problem into finding the maximum number of overlapping intervals on a line. This involves projecting the circles onto a line and counting overlaps efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406507.518236
      },
      "rev_n_3_e9d5be_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_e9d5be_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_e9d5be",
        "thought_text": "Apply a divide-and-conquer strategy to recursively divide the set of circles into smaller subsets, solve the problem for each subset, and then combine the results. This can potentially reduce the complexity compared to a brute-force approach.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406507.518255
      },
      "rev_n_4_53a78f_0": {
