        "node_id": "n_13_8f4867",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the angle calculation by iterating over a smaller set of angles. Instead of considering every possible angle between two points, limit the angles to a fixed number of divisions around the circle (e.g., 360 degrees). This reduces the computational complexity while still capturing the most likely optimal angles.",
